 "briefing": "# Stripe Briefing: Changes from 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Summary\n\nNo verified changes at Stripe for 16 October to 15 November 2026 could be sourced. Every search attempt failed with a rate-limit error, so no news items, product launches, executive moves, or deals were confirmed with a dated, primary or reputable source. Under the sourcing rules for this briefing, no unverified facts are included. Before the 17 November meeting, the primary sources listed under \"Where to Verify\" should be checked directly.\n\n## News\n\nNo company news for the window has been verified. This covers financial results, valuation or tender offer activity, regulatory or legal developments, leadership statements, country expansion, outages, and restructuring.\n\n## Product Launches\n\nNo product launches, feature releases, API or platform changes, deprecations, or incidents for the window have been verified across any business area, including payments, Billing, Connect, Issuing, Treasury, Terminal, Radar, Identity, Tax, Capital, Link, stablecoins, agentic commerce, or Checkout.\n\n## Hires and Departures\n\nNo executive hires, promotions, or departures for the window have been verified.\n\n## Deals\n\nNo acquisitions, partnerships, investments, funding rounds, Form D filings, or major customer or contract announcements for the window have been verified.\n\n## Where to Verify Before the Meeting\n\nThe following primary sources should be checked for announcements dated 16 October to 15 November 2026. They are listed as places to verify, not as evidence of any change:\n\n- Stripe newsroom for press releases and announcements [1]\n- Stripe blog for product and company posts [2]\n- Stripe status page for incidents and maintenance [3]\n- Stripe API changelog for version and product changes [4]\n- SEC EDGAR for any filings that name Stripe [5]\n\nReputable outlets such as Reuters, Bloomberg, the Financial Times, TechCrunch, and The Information should also be searched for \"Stripe\" with terms such as \"appoints,\" \"acquires,\" \"launches,\" and \"partners\" for the same window.\n\n## Open Questions for the Meeting\n\nThese questions are not tied to verified changes, because none could be confirmed. They are framed around the areas where a change would matter most to a meeting with Stripe. Once the primary sources above are checked, they should be revised to reflect any changes found.\n\n1. Which product or API changes made in the last month should our team plan around, and where are they documented in the changelog?\n2. Have there been any changes to the teams, leaders, or account contacts we would work with, and who will be our main point of contact going forward?\n3. Are there any changes to pricing, payment method availability, country coverage, or stablecoin and agentic commerce programs that would affect our roadmap for the coming quarter?\n\n## Sources\n\n[1] Stripe Newsroom: https://stripe.com/newsroom\n[2] Stripe Blog: https://stripe.com/blog\n[3] Stripe Status: https://status.stripe.com\n[4] Stripe API Changelog: https://docs.stripe.com/changelog\n[5] SEC EDGAR Company Search: https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/",
